-- Companion example for row 3 of "Five Kinds of No Answer" (non-answers.md):
-- a fact nobody has supplied yet.
--
-- Run it with:  l4 run non-answers-not-yet-known.l4
--
-- It lives in its own file because it uses the section GIVEN, and the other
-- five rows of the page live in non-answers-example.l4.

§ `3. A fact nobody has supplied yet -- a section GIVEN`
    GIVEN `the applicant's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Age at the date of the claim

-- Alex's age is the case's contribution, not the law's. The file names the
-- blank; whoever brings a case fills it in.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is of pensionable age` MEANS
    `the applicant's age in years` AT LEAST 65

-- L4 accepts the rule whether or not anyone has filled the blank. #CHECK asks
-- what kind of answer the rule gives, without working the answer out: a
-- yes-or-no fact, BOOLEAN.
--
-- Asking for the answer itself with #EVAL would stop and name the blank. That
-- message is quoted on the page; it cannot be shown here, because a file under
-- doc/ has to run cleanly.
#CHECK `is of pensionable age`
